<title>CHILE: Chile January financial sector earnings rise.</title>
<headline>Chile January financial sector earnings rise.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's banking and financial sector reported earnings of 23.9 billion pesos in January, up 11.2 percent on the same month last year, said the Banks and Financial Institutions Superintendency.</p>
<p>The figures showed the sector's profits falling 24 percent from December.</p>
<p>Loan portfolios rose 10.4 percent last month. Commercial loans were up 11.6 percent on January 1996, while consumer loans climbed a strong 33 percent.</p>
<p>The following are the net earnings of individual banks in January.</p>
<p>				     Jan 1997		Jan 1996</p>
<p>Bhif			  1.02		    n/a</p>
<p>Banco de A. Edwards    1.85		    1.74</p>
<p>Banco de Chile	 5.84		    n/a</p>
<p>Banco de Credito e Inv 1.99		    n/a</p>
<p>Banco Santiago	   2.29		    n/a</p>
<p>Banco Santander-Chile  3.25		    n/a</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in billions of pesos. The 1996 figures are in peso terms from that year and are not expressed in 1997 pesos.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212))</p>
